{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310600,"nonce":"btQ2t/yfE4LZuZYF4K3ooXW+bRo=","title":"OPEN: a call returning an ERASED type parameter, passed straight as an argument, is treated as a pointer — `Sys.println(x.evaluate())` ...","message":"```haxe\nabstract Lazy\u003cT\u003e(()-\u003eT) {\n    public function new(f) this = f;\n    public function evaluate() return this();\n    @:from static function ofConst\u003cT\u003e(c:T):Lazy\u003cT\u003e return new Lazy(function() return c);\n}\nclass Main {\n    static function lazy\u003cA\u003e(l:Lazy\u003cA\u003e):Lazy\u003cA\u003e return l;\n    static function main() {\n        var fInt = lazy(2);\n        Sys.println(fInt.evaluate());      // rayzor: exit 139. haxe: 2\n        // var v:Int = fInt.evaluate(); Sys.println(v == 2);  // WORKS\n    }\n}\n```\nMIR at the crash (`scratchpad/sigbus/Plain.hx`):\n```\n$9  = call fn4($4)          ; evaluate, declared `-\u003e ?T`\n$10 = cast i64 $9 to *void  ; the Int 2 becomes a pointer\ncall fn7($10)               ; println dereferences it\n```\n`evaluate`'s MIR return type prints as `?T` — the type parameter survives to MIR\nuninstantiated, so the argument position picks the pointer representation. Binding\nto a declared local first fixes it, which is why Plain2.hx passes.\n\nThis is what remains of the Lazy chain after [[bugs_abstract_over_closure_from_sigsegv]]\nlayers 1-3 were fixed (a52173d2, e9d9a431, and the inline guard). Same family as\nbugs_std_string_dynamic_unbox_and_erased_generics.\n\n- Index summary moved from MEMORY.md (2026-10-18): OPEN: a call returning erased `T` passed DIRECTLY as an arg becomes `cast i64 -\u003e *void` ⇒ SIGSEGV. Bind to a typed local to work around. MIR evidence inside.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_erased_generic_return_as_call_argument` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}